# ARMSX3: the repo root .gitignore has a blanket `*.so` rule (it is upstream
# RPCS3's, meant for build output). That rule silently swallowed ARMSX2's bundled
# ANGLE libraries: they never reached the release staging directory, the APK
# shipped without them, and the core fell back to the system GLES driver in
# silence - which read to users as "ANGLE is broken" and could not be diagnosed
# from a log.
#
# So the ANGLE libraries are un-ignored EXPLICITLY here, by name. They are
# redistributable prebuilts (ANGLE is BSD-3-Clause), not build output, and they
# have to be in version control for the APK to be reproducible.
#
# Everything else under jniLibs/ stays ignored: libarmsx3-core.so and
# librashader.so are genuinely build products, staged at build time.
!arm64-v8a/libEGL_angle.so
!arm64-v8a/libGLESv2_angle.so
